# WNBA Model Dashboard

Next.js 16 + Neon (Postgres) dashboard for a WNBA player prop model.
Live at https://wnba-model-five.vercel.app

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Neon (serverless Postgres) via `@neondatabase/serverless`
- Deployed on Vercel (auto-deploys on push to main)
- No component library - all UI is hand-rolled with inline styles using CSS variables

## Project structure

src/
  app/
    today/page.tsx        - Today's scan (server component, revalidate 300s)
    tomorrow/page.tsx     - Tomorrow's scan
    yesterday/page.tsx    - Yesterday's scan
    tracker/page.tsx      - Bet Tracker with KPI cards
    history/page.tsx      - All scan history grouped by date
    api/
      placed-bets/route.ts  - POST/DELETE/PATCH for bet tracking (checkbox -> DB)
  components/
    Nav.tsx               - Sticky top nav
    ScanPage.tsx          - Server component: fetches data, renders ScanTable
    ScanTable.tsx         - Client component: the bet table + checkbox interaction
    Drawer.tsx            - Slide-in detail panel per bet
    TierBadge.tsx         - S/A/B/C/D/F colored tier badge
  lib/
    db.ts                 - Neon connection (sql tagged template)
    queries.ts            - All DB reads (wrapped in try/catch, return [] on error)
    types.ts              - Shared TypeScript types + helpers (edgeTier, formatOdds, etc.)
    dates.ts              - todayET(), tomorrowET(), yesterdayET() in US Eastern
    schema.sql            - Postgres schema (run once via psql or Neon SQL editor)

## Database tables (Neon)

- `scan_snapshots` - model scan output, written by Python propmodel on every scan
- `placed_bets` - bets the user checked off; written by /api/placed-bets in real time
- `bet_journal` - CLV tracking, written by Python propmodel after games close

## Design system

Dark sports-analytics theme. CSS variables defined in globals.css:
- --bg, --bg-card, --bg-card-hover, --border, --text-primary, --text-secondary, --text-muted, --accent
- Tier colors: --tier-s (#a78bfa), --tier-a (#34d399), --tier-b (#60a5fa), --tier-c (#fbbf24), --tier-d (#fb923c), --tier-f (#f87171)
- Side colors: --over (#60a5fa), --under (#fb923c)
- Result colors: --won (#34d399), --lost (#f87171)

Tier thresholds (in types.ts edgeTier()):
  S >= 15%, A >= 12%, B >= 9%, C >= 7%, D >= 5%, F < 5%

## Key conventions

- All DB queries live in lib/queries.ts and return empty arrays on error (build never fails)
- Pages are server components; interactivity (checkboxes, drawer) lives in client components
- Bet tracking: checkbox click -> fetch /api/placed-bets -> instant DB write, no sync scripts
- Dates are always US Eastern. Use dates.ts helpers, never raw new Date() for game dates.
- stat labels: points=PTS, rebounds=REB, assists=AST, strikeouts_pitcher=K, earned_runs=ER
- book labels: draftkings=DK, fanduel=FD, caesars=CZR, novig=NV

## Data flow

Python propmodel (separate repo: bet-model) runs scans -> writes to Neon scan_snapshots
-> Next.js reads scan_snapshots -> displays in dashboard
User checks checkbox -> /api/placed-bets writes to placed_bets -> Bet Tracker reads it
Python resolves games -> writes to bet_journal -> Bet Tracker joins and shows CLV/result

## Environment

DATABASE_URL is set in .env.local (from Vercel via `vercel env pull .env.local`).
Never commit .env.local. Never hardcode credentials.
